{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/257637-5-dot-token-two-man-coat","id":257637,"title":"5 Dot Token: Two-Man Coat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-15T15:13:45-07:00","id":257637,"title":"5 Dot Token: Two-Man Coat","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">I made this a long while back and thought I'd share. Let me know what you think!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Two Man Coat: 5 dot Token</span><br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3 glamour + 1 willpower point from both changelings involved<br /> <br /> At first glance, this over sized trench coat looks too big for anyone one person to wear. But when two changelings wear it correctly, they merge their bodies together to form a single changeling that shares characteristics of the two involved. The details on which traits are apparent depend on multiple factors. Both participants must decide who plays \u201ctop\u201d and who plays \u201cbottom.\u201d<br /> The Changeling on top, when the token is used, acts as the head and speaker for the two, while the bottom Changeling acts as the rest of the body, and has total control over the limbs. The overall size and weight of the fused changeling is also equal to that of the larger participant.<br /> Even if not apparent, the two Changelings involved can telepathically communicate with each other, and are both able to see and feel what the other does. However, only the top Changeling may speak vocally. The token deactivates upon removal of the coat (which takes the altered appearance of the both sets of clothes the changelings are wearing).<br /> Usage of this token grants a +3 to disguise checks, while the physical attributes of the gestalt is defined by the highest between the two participants. Any contracts known by the two may be cast, but any glamour expenditure is made by the owner of said-contract. Finally, the coat itself can transform into any set of clothing (though its armor rating remains the same). The only condition to this power is that part of the getup divides the body around the waist or torso (such as a sash, pair of pants, or similar). Removing such clothing causes it to disappear, but can be &quot;returned&quot; as a reflexive action.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Usage of the token requires both participants to willingly agree to the process. Furthermore, the coat may cause the participants to share memories and derangements the longer the two remain fused. The Storyteller is welcome to interpret this, and any other issues not already noted, as they see fit.<br /> <br /> (Alternatively, the drawback could be that the gestalt changeling is very easy to sense due to the massive amounts of glamour keeping the two fused.)<br /> <br /> <b>Catch:</b> the participants must drink at least 7 tea spoons worth of the other's blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fun suggestions:</b><br /> <br /> 1. With Mirror 4 - Odd Body, you can create a mouth for the bottom half to speak through, for bonus points, make it across the belly.<br /> 2. Using Contracts of Mirror to transform into your normal, everyday self is fully permissible, and a great way to catch the enemy off guard. The tiny wizened suddenly has the strength of an ogre?!<br /> 3. Play tests have proven this to be a popular token to use with ingame life-partners, be they male, female, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 09-16-2014, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T18:13:04-07:00","id":257726,"title":"","content":"I like this idea a lot, as it adds an element of terror to the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0bPjUz9X8I8\" target=\"_blank\">Muppet Man</a> gag. It needs a LOT more mechanical oomph, though; currently the only advantage +3 to disguises. Sure it's cool to smuggle someone past a bouncer or something, but it's definitely not worth 5 dots.<br /> <br /> One suggestion I have to beef this up: stack the participants' Physical Ability ratings (which can be a boon to Contracts), but use the higher of the Health ratings. Maybe even give them temporary +1 Health because they're basically twice the person. Damage gets split between the wearers when the coat is removed.<br /> <br /> Other things I would do is stipulate that they have access to all Contracts possessed between them, but the owner of said Contract still pays out of his or her Glamour pool (Glamour is not combined). Perhaps they also get to use the higher of any of the Skill ratings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T18:27:00-07:00","id":257734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/257637-5-dot-token-two-man-coat?p=257726#post257726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this idea a lot, as it adds an element of terror to the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0bPjUz9X8I8\" target=\"_blank\">Muppet Man</a> gag. It needs a LOT more mechanical oomph, though; currently the only advantage +3 to disguises. Sure it's cool to smuggle someone past a bouncer or something, but it's definitely not worth 5 dots.<br /> <br /> One suggestion I have to beef this up: stack the participants' Physical Ability ratings (which can be a boon to Contracts), but use the higher of the Health ratings. Maybe even give them temporary +1 Health because they're basically twice the person. Damage gets split between the wearers when the coat is removed.<br /> <br /> Other things I would do is stipulate that they have access to all Contracts possessed between them, but the owner of said Contract still pays out of his or her Glamour pool (Glamour is not combined). Perhaps they also get to use the higher of any of the Skill ratings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dammit, I thought I wrote that it. Guess I forgot to update. Uhh--here, tell me what you think <b><i>now.</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T00:27:40-07:00","id":263500,"title":"","content":"You know what else I like about this? How it subtly pushes the users into person after a time. Heck, it's not even covert about it! It does just what it says on the tin.<br /> <br /> So all the Physical Attributes stack between the two participants. That's good! But what about the Mental and Social ones? The Mental Attributes I imagine come straight from the &quot;head&quot; Changeling, but Social ones are a bit trickier. How have you handled that in your game so far?<br /> <br /> And whose Skills do you end up using? I would say the split means that all Physical Skills come straight from the &quot;Bottom&quot; Changeling, and that both of them can make Mental Skill rolls, but again Social is a fuzzy gray area.<br /> <br /> Also: I would definitely specify that Mr. Twobody here only gets one turn. He's still only one man, after all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You know, going by the effects I would also say this is a 4-dot Token (maybe even 3!). 5-dot Tokens tend to have even broader implications and effect several people at once, and while the Coat is certainly potent and makes a heavy hitter, they don't have the amazing versatility or world-wrecking capabilities that canon 5-dot Tokens do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T09:42:30-07:00","id":263873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/257637-5-dot-token-two-man-coat?p=263500#post263500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what else I like about this? How it subtly pushes the users into person after a time. Heck, it's not even covert about it! It does just what it says on the tin.<br /> <br /> So all the Physical Attributes stack between the two participants. That's good! But what about the Mental and Social ones? The Mental Attributes I imagine come straight from the &quot;head&quot; Changeling, but Social ones are a bit trickier. How have you handled that in your game so far?<br /> <br /> And whose Skills do you end up using? I would say the split means that all Physical Skills come straight from the &quot;Bottom&quot; Changeling, and that both of them can make Mental Skill rolls, but again Social is a fuzzy gray area.<br /> <br /> Also: I would definitely specify that Mr. Twobody here only gets one turn. He's still only one man, after all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You know, going by the effects I would also say this is a 4-dot Token (maybe even 3!). 5-dot Tokens tend to have even broader implications and effect several people at once, and while the Coat is certainly potent and makes a heavy hitter, they don't have the amazing versatility or world-wrecking capabilities that canon 5-dot Tokens do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, besides having a lot of neat benefits and tricks, the 5-dot marker is meant to emphasize its rarity and difficulty in replicating. If it were easy, every freehold would have one (or more). That could prove overpowering, if it didn't ruin the novelty of the token itself. In the hands of two powerful Lost, it could make a super-changeling!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T07:23:51-08:00","id":325994,"title":"","content":"Tiny Turret: &quot;Are you still there?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}